---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Static Pulse Sites | Business Systems Studio"
  description="Learn how Static Pulse Sites helps small and medium businesses simplify operations through websites, automation, and custom internal software."
>
  <main>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Technology should support the way your business works.</h1>

        <p class="lead hero-lead">
          Static Pulse Sites is a Business Systems Studio that helps small and
          medium businesses improve their websites, connect their tools,
          automate repetitive processes, and build focused internal software.
        </p>

        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">
            Start Your Project
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container about-hero">
        <div>
          <h2>Why Static Pulse Sites exists.</h2>

          <p>
            Static Pulse Sites began with website development after founder
            Daniela Carrion experienced firsthand how difficult it can be to
            manage a website built on a fragile, plugin-dependent platform.
          </p>

          <p>
            Learning how websites work beneath the surface led to a broader
            realization: many businesses face the same problem across their
            entire operation. They have several tools, but those tools do not
            work together. Important processes still depend on spreadsheets,
            manual follow-up, copied information, and disconnected systems.
          </p>

          <p>
            The company evolved into a Business Systems Studio to address that
            larger problem. Today, Static Pulse Sites combines website
            development, automation, and custom internal software to help
            businesses create simpler and more connected ways of working.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="about-photo-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/ceo-photo.png"
            alt="Daniela Carrion, founder of Static Pulse Sites"
            class="about-photo"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2>Business needs come before technology.</h2>

          <p class="lead">
            We do not begin projects by choosing a platform, adding AI, or
            recommending new software. We begin by understanding the problem,
            the people involved, and the outcome the business needs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-3">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Simplicity</h3>
            <p>
              Technology should reduce complexity rather than add more systems
              for your team to manage.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <h3>Ownership</h3>
            <p>
              Clients retain ownership of their websites, software, source
              code, and business data.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <h3>Practical AI</h3>
            <p>
              AI is introduced only when it creates useful and measurable value
              within a real workflow.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <h3>Human Guidance</h3>
            <p>
              Every project includes direct collaboration and clear
              explanations without expecting clients to understand code.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <h3>Focused Solutions</h3>
            <p>
              We solve the defined business problem instead of adding features
              that do not support the outcome.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <h3>Long-Term Flexibility</h3>
            <p>
              Systems are built so they can evolve as the business, team, and
              process change.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2>A collaborative process from problem to launch.</h2>

          <p class="lead">
            Clients do not need to know which technology they need before
            contacting us. Our role is to understand the business and recommend
            the simplest practical solution.
          </p>
        </div>

        <ol class="process-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Start with the problem.</strong>
            You explain what is slowing the business down or what needs to
            improve.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>Understand the process.</strong>
            We review the people, tools, information, and steps involved.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>Design the solution.</strong>
            We define the most appropriate website, automation, software, or
            combination.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>Build with feedback.</strong>
            You review the work throughout the project rather than waiting
            until the end.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>Launch and support.</strong>
            We help put the system into use and continue improving it when
            needed.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="cta-box">
          <h2>Tell us what you want your business to do more efficiently.</h2>

          <p class="lead">
            You do not need to arrive with a technical plan. Start by
            describing the problem, the current process, and the result you
            want.
          </p>

          <div class="button-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">
              Start Your Project
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>